    {
      "phase": "variables-publish-refusal-before-rename",
      "bodyText": "GraphGoblin\nChat\nLoops\nRuns\nEvents\nSettings\nUndo edit variables\nRedo\nLoops\n/\nHeld variables same-window control\ndraft only\nAll changes saved\nOpen in Runs\nPublish the loop first: runs start from a published version.\n1 error, 1 warning\nPublish\n\nPublish failed\n\nSome fields hold input that is not a valid value yet; complete or discard it first.\nPalette\nTrigger\nStarts a run\nDecision\nChooses a route and can limit repeats\nInference\nHands work to a harness\nScript\nRuns a program\nMutate\nChanges the context thread\nSubloop\nRuns another loop\nWait\nParks until input, time, or a signal\nHeartbeat\nPolls on an interval\nExit\nFinishes with an outcome and return value\nY…\nNo\nTRIGGER\nStart\nstart\nout\nDECISION\nPick\npick\nYes\nNo\nINFERENCE\nWork\nwork\nout\nEXIT\nDone\ndone\nEXIT\nOther\nother\nReact Flow\nLoop settings\n\nRequired fields are marked *\n\nName\n*\nDescription\nSETTINGS\n\nMaximum node visits is a safety cap against unintended cycles. Use a decision gate's maximum passes for an intentional repeat. The elapsed execution deadline includes waits and pauses. There is no run deadline unless you set one. Structured completion milliseconds bounds each LLM decision evaluation or output-transform repair through the structured port when Limited; it defaults to Unlimited. Same-session inference schema repairs follow the node timeout. Visits and passes can also be explicitly set to Unlimited; cancellation remains available.\n\nWorking directory\nKind\nfixed\ntemplate\ntemp\nTemplate\n*\nLiquid\n1\n/tmp/{{ outputs.work.value }}\nPreview (sample thread): /tmp/\nDefaults\nBy harness\n\nDefaults keyed by their harness; omitted fields inherit only within that harness.\n\nAdd entry\nMaximum node visits\nLimited\nUnlimited\n\nFresh entries per node. Default 10; unlimited removes this cutoff.\n\nRun deadline seconds\nLimited\nNo run deadline\n\nElapsed seconds including waits, pauses and restart downtime. No deadline by default; set seconds to add one.\n\nNo deadline; set one to stop a forgotten run.\n\nStructured completion milliseconds\nLimited\nUnlimited\n\nMilliseconds per LLM decision evaluation or output-transform repair through the structured port. Same-session inference schema repairs follow the node timeout. No deadline by default; Unlimited removes this cutoff.\n\nNo completion deadline; LLM decisions and repairs remain cancellable.\n\nSubloop depth limit\nVARIABLES\n\nEach variable maps a name to a JSON Schema.\n\nVariables *\nKey\nValue\n*\nJSON\n1\n[1, \n\nInvalid JSON: Unexpected end of JSON input\nDiscard the unparsed text\n\nAdd entry",
      "writes": [
        {
          "phase": "original",
          "method": "POST",
          "path": "/loops/<loop>/validate"
        }
      ]
    },
